  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 202 PM MDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nFriday...Will see an abrupt cutoff to the low and mid level moisture \nsupply as drier air at low and mid levels advects into our counties \nas the dominant ridge over Colorado and southern Wyoming reasserts \nitself. Thus dry and hotter.\n\nSaturday through Tuesday...Isolated to scattered afternoon and \nevening showers and thunderstorms expected, with areal coverage \nincreasing each day due to increased mid level moisture. \nFortunately, more beneficial rains expected concentrated over and \nnear our Snowy, Sierra Madre and Laramie Ranges, with the best \nchances for convection on Monday and Tuesday. Typical weak northwest \nflow aloft on the northeast periphery of the ridge aloft will aid in \noccasional passing shortwave troughs aloft near peak heating \nresulting in increasing convective potential each day",
